  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "Even with Margulis super-rigidity for the smaller lattice and Furstenberg’s measurable-map theorem as named prerequisites, the authors must establish source-local H-orbit constancy without assuming that the ambient discrete group is a lattice. The retained local argument constructs a single-orbit map, propagates its invariance through finitely many Zariski-dense conjugates of H to all of G, and uses the non-archimedean probability-measure stabilizer alternative to force compact image. This passage from a smaller higher-rank lattice to an ambient discrete group is research-level rigidity beyond ordinary PhD qualification exercises.",
